      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nOrders like this should also come from a licensed prescriber, or be verified by one. If you're relaying the order for a clinician, please have them confirm the intended dose.\n\nOnce I have a confirmed dose, I can enter it right away. For example, the usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg by mouth once daily, and the usual range is 50\u2013200 mg once daily. If the dose really is 1000 mg, the prescriber should confirm that directly and add their rationale. I'd also suggest a pharmacist review before the order goes in."
