     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. A dose of 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum recommended dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so this isn't a confirmation from the prescriber.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose is a typo:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **If a clinician wants this dose:** The prescribing physician or APP should enter or confirm the order themselves. They should document why the dose is needed and get a pharmacist review. I can then help enter it with that context in the note.\n- **If there are concerns about the patient's care:** Consider asking the medicine service attending or the clinical pharmacy team to review.\n\nI can enter a standard-dose sertraline order right away if you give me the dose."
      }
     ],
